### M'Ensemble API — every route, in the order you'd walk them.
###
### Works in VS Code (REST Client) and JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Run the two logins first: they capture the tokens the rest of the file uses.
###
### Seeded credentials — everyone's password is `mensemble`.
###   yusuf@example.com  user_001  member, follows Khadija + Madina
###   amina@example.com  user_002  coordinator @ Khadija

@host = http://localhost:4000/api
@mosque = mosque_khadija
@post = post_001

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── open ───

### Liveness. `db` should read "connected"; check the server log says m_ensemble.
GET {{host}}/health

### Create an account. 201 → { token, user }. Password floor is 6.
POST {{host}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "new.person@example.com", "password": "hunter22", "name": "Nadia" }

### Sign in as a member. Captures @member.
# @name memberLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "yusuf@example.com", "password": "mensemble" }

@member = {{memberLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### Sign in as the Khadija coordinator. Captures @admin.
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "amina@example.com", "password": "mensemble" }

@admin = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### Wrong password → 401 BAD_CREDENTIALS. Same body as an unknown email.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "yusuf@example.com", "password": "wrong" }

### No bearer → 401 UNAUTHORIZED. This status is what signs the app out.
GET {{host}}/me

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── me ───

### The wire shape is exactly { _id, name, email, interests, pushToken? }.
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Onboarding writes interests through here.
PATCH {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "interests": ["Volunteering", "Community meals", "Youth"] }

### Anything but name/interests/pushToken → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
PATCH {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "hijack@example.com" }

### Runs on every cold start; decides which shell the session lands in.
GET {{host}}/me/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Mosques the user follows.
GET {{host}}/me/mosques
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Confirmed signups, all time — the app splits past from upcoming.
GET {{host}}/me/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Every checked-in signup, ANY post type. (The dashboard counts volunteer only.)
GET {{host}}/me/hours
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

GET {{host}}/me/notification-prefs
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Whole replace — all five booleans required.
PUT {{host}}/me/notification-prefs
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "volunteerRequests": true,
  "events": true,
  "classes": true,
  "announcements": true,
  "prayerReminders": false
}

### Idempotent; called on every launch.
POST {{host}}/me/push-token
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "ExponentPushToken[xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]" }

### Names for a signup list. Never email. Unknown ids drop silently.
GET {{host}}/users?ids=user_001,user_002,user_999
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### An empty list is 200 [], not a 400.
GET {{host}}/users?ids=
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────── mosques ───

GET {{host}}/mosques
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Idempotent both ways.
POST {{host}}/mosques/mosque_rawdah/follow
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

DELETE {{host}}/mosques/mosque_rawdah/follow
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Live posts only: not cancelled, not over. startAt ascending.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Everything incl. past and cancelled — admin only.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/posts?all=true
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Same URL as a member → 403 FORBIDDEN.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/posts?all=true
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── prayer ───

### Adhan computed from the mosque's coordinates; iqamah from its own config.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/prayer-times?date=2026-09-06
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Madina Isha is fixed at 21:15 from 2026-09-08 — null the day before.
GET {{host}}/mosques/mosque_madina/prayer-times?date=2026-09-07
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

GET {{host}}/mosques/mosque_madina/prayer-times?date=2026-09-08
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Any signed-in user. Note: no _id on the rows, so the editor can echo them back.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/iqamah
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Whole replace. The app re-sends historical rows itself, so this is not lossy.
PUT {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/iqamah
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "iqamah": [
    { "prayer": "fajr", "mode": "fixed", "fixedTime": "05:45", "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01" },
    { "prayer": "dhuhr", "mode": "fixed", "fixedTime": "13:30", "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01" },
    { "prayer": "asr", "mode": "offset", "offsetMinutes": 15, "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01" },
    { "prayer": "maghrib", "mode": "offset", "offsetMinutes": 5, "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01" },
    { "prayer": "isha", "mode": "fixed", "fixedTime": "21:30", "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01" }
  ],
  "jummah": [
    { "label": "First jummah", "khutbahTime": "13:00", "iqamahTime": "13:20" },
    { "label": "Second jummah", "khutbahTime": "14:15", "iqamahTime": "14:35" }
  ]
}

### ───────────────────────────────────────────── feed & posts ───

### Scope is the mosques you follow unless ?mosques= says otherwise.
GET {{host}}/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

GET {{host}}/feed?types=volunteer,event
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Browsing another city: ?mosques wins over what you follow.
GET {{host}}/feed?mosques=mosque_ottawa,mosque_toronto
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Any post, any mosque — "My Stuff" hydrates saved posts through here.
GET {{host}}/posts/{{post}}
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### All statuses; the app filters `confirmed` itself.
GET {{host}}/posts/{{post}}/signups
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### The atomic claim. 201 → Signup. Repeat → 409 ALREADY_SIGNED_UP.
### Full → 409 FULL. Cancelled → 410 with code NOT_FOUND.
POST {{host}}/posts/{{post}}/signup
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Gives the slot back, floored at 0. 404 if there was nothing confirmed.
DELETE {{host}}/posts/{{post}}/signup
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### Self check-in — the QR flow. Needs a confirmed signup first.
POST {{host}}/posts/{{post}}/checkin
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "user_001" }

### A coordinator may check anyone in; another member gets 403.
POST {{host}}/posts/{{post}}/checkin
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "user_001" }

### Admin of body.mosqueId. Fans a push out to matching followers afterwards.
# @name createPost
POST {{host}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mosqueId": "mosque_khadija",
  "type": "volunteer",
  "title": "Iftar setup — four people needed",
  "description": "Tables, water jugs, and the serving line.",
  "category": "Community meals",
  "startAt": "2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z",
  "endAt": "2026-09-12T23:30:00.000Z",
  "location": "Main hall, basement level",
  "slotsNeeded": 4
}

@newPost = {{createPost.response.body.data._id}}

### Type and mosqueId are fixed at creation — either → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
PATCH {{host}}/posts/{{newPost}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "event" }

PATCH {{host}}/posts/{{newPost}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Iftar setup — now five people", "slotsNeeded": 5 }

### Idempotent. The post leaves the feed but keeps its history.
POST {{host}}/posts/{{newPost}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Signing up for it now → 410, code NOT_FOUND.
POST {{host}}/posts/{{newPost}}/signup
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}

### A member creating a post → 403 FORBIDDEN.
POST {{host}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{member}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mosqueId": "mosque_khadija",
  "type": "announcement",
  "title": "Nope",
  "description": "",
  "category": "Outreach",
  "startAt": "2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z",
  "endAt": "2026-09-30T23:59:00.000Z",
  "location": "Mosque"
}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── admin ───

### Every number on the coordinator's home, in one round trip.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### The list you work from on the day.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/roster?upcoming=true
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/roster?types=volunteer&post={{post}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Followers ∪ role-holders ∪ anyone who ever signed up. Admins sort first.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/members/user_001
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Upserts the Membership row and never touches Follow.
PUT {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/members/user_001/role
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### Demoting yourself → 403 FORBIDDEN: it would lock you out of this screen.
PUT {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/members/user_002/role
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "member" }

### Ended posts, announcements excluded, newest first.
GET {{host}}/mosques/{{mosque}}/outcomes
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
